        <body>
            <div xml:id="d419">

                <pb facs="0743" n="623" sameAs="frus:frus1932v01/pg623"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 Great Britain/293: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain (Atherton) to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1932-03-29T19:00:00+00:00">March 29, 1932—7
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 29—3:15 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>122. Upon informal inquiry of Treasury official (Department’s 98, December [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">March</hi>] 26, 2 p.m.) I was informed that with the <pb
                        facs="0744" n="624" xml:id="pg624"/> postponement of the Lausanne Conference
                    until June, Treasury had delayed advisedly designating a representative and it
                    was added informally “should it not appear discourteous to the United States
                    Government, Treasury negotiations would be considerably aided if further delay
                    might be permitted until after Lausanne Conference.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Atherton</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
